From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mindw0rk <alex@evgrafov.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:49:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cloud saves: the Mac and iPhone apps of a game play on from
 one save through an iCloud Drive folder

Until now a save moved between the Mac and an iPhone only by hand (the Mac front end's Saves sheet, over the cable). The apps are signed ad hoc or with a free/personal team, so CloudKit and iCloud entitlements are out; a folder the player picks in iCloud Drive is not.

dm/host/save_sync.c packs the committed save (DM_SAVE and DM_SAVE_device) into one file, <folder>/<title ID>/save.dmsync (a folder named after the title ID is taken as the game's own), because iCloud replaces a file as a whole but syncs a folder file by file. The cloud's copy comes in at the game's first save mount, before the work directory is cloned; the committed save goes out a few seconds after a Commit on a thread of its own, when the iPhone app goes to the background, and from the Mac launcher once the host has exited. <DM_SAVE>.sync keeps the hash of the save last known to be the same on both sides: only the cloud's changed, it comes in; only this one changed, it goes out; both changed, the newer wins. Every save this replaces, here or in the cloud, is kept first in <DM_SAVE>-backups/<date> local|cloud.

The folder is chosen in each app's launcher: Cloud saves in the Mac settings window (dm/mac/Launcher.swift, defaults key cloudSaves.folder, read by launcher.c) and on the iPhone (a security-scoped bookmark, DataBookmark.m). DM_SAVE_SYNC (a folder, icloud, or 0) overrides both. On the iPhone the copies go through NSFileCoordinator (SaveSync.m), which downloads a file iCloud has only listed.

Tested: dm/host/tests/t_save_sync.c (47 checks, also under TSan and ASan/UBSan), and TOTK 1.4.3 between an iPhone and a Mac in both directions.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#617
Reason: Cross-save between a game's Mac and iPhone apps through an iCloud Drive folder the player picks (CloudKit needs entitlements these signings do not have)
Issue: none yet
